nature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f66bbd29d7b34bd3dc2b986cc8a1a61ba96ddee1c1ec146c8168811d85973d3c","event_uuid":"709d1c27-2834-4672-9024-4c69c6251ada","position":{"commit_sha":"63fd5d15122034f08e72c92d4c8ab5b28ab191d1","position":"1787441837261404001-709d1c27-2834-4672-9024-4c69c6251ada"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dc42d35223d2ae4a0235fd6eae1236b565ec252ed8e72d5ea3a82c8f035502ae","event_uuid":"cb865831-0ef0-4190-ba35-890785a6d027","position":{"commit_sha":"d1c6cfae8d6ad0f91e1716f3584b706f9ad29fd5","position":"1787441852527391001-cb865831-0ef0-4190-ba35-890785a6d027"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2122 (commit 2e2dc69c123). Plan-review PASSED and was signed (ironically the attestation initially failed to persist under tracker churn — bug a83f-6348's exact starvation — and was recovered via rebar sign-review). RED->GREEN held-out tests added to tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py: transient store-read-failure retries then signs (calls==2); persistent failure exhausts MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS into a structured retry-after-repair refusal; deterministic malformed-reference refuses on the first attempt. make lint, make typecheck, complexity ratchet (new=0 increased=0) all green. Note: tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py::test_resign_routes_through_pin_collecting_sign_path times out locally on UNMODIFIED HEAD too (materialize_tickets against the real shared tracker with repo_root=None) — environmental, not introduced by this change. caused_by analysis: git log -L on the resign baseline-collect region -> introduced by 94e605a29d2 (ticket 5967-4476-7f9f-442d, 'Add phased plan-review attestations'), same origin ec1e attributed its half to; ec1e's fix scoped itself to sign_manifest and filed this ticket as discovered_from rather than shipping past an obligation, so attribution goes to resign's originating ticket: caused_by=5967-4476-7f9f-442d, class=plan_defect (same asymmetric terminal handling of a normal concurrency transient, from the same commit).","timestamp":1787434142575357001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLOSE EVIDENCE — Gerrit change 2122 MERGED as 7825673f867 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved comments; server-side rebase of 2e2dc69c123, Change-Id Ica2a71e6e13b5b237490aa7d364ffbe2c97beb5c).\n\nAC-1 (transient retried then signs): tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py::test_transient_store_read_failure_is_retried_then_resign_signs — RED on pre-fix code (terminal \"could not be collected\" refusal), GREEN post-fix; asserts collect called twice and ok=True/signed=True.\nAC-2 (persistent exhausts into structured retry-after-repair refusal): heldout test asserts exactly generation.MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS collect attempts and an ok=False refusal naming the transient store-read-failure and advising a sign-review retry.\nAC-3 (deterministic reasons terminal on first attempt): heldout test with malformed-reference asserts a single attempt and the terminal refusal.\nAC-4 (gates): make lint, make typecheck (mypy: no issues in 638 files), python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check new=0 increased=0 — all green locally at 2e2dc69c123 and in CI (Verified +1 on the merged patchset).\n\nPost-merge re-validation in this worktree at origin/main (4e2b4dfb3cf): pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_sign_transaction.py -> 14 passed.\n\nDisposition: class=plan_defect, caused_by=5967-4476-7f9f-442d — git log -L over the resign baseline-collect region walks carriers 032f30fdc83 (c083) and a475e24fc9c back to 94e605a29d2 (\"Add phased plan-review attestations\", rebar-ticket: 5967-4476-7f9f-442d), which introduced the one-shot collect inside the broad terminal except; ec1e's fix (change 2118) deliberately scoped itself to sign_manifest and filed this ticket discovered_from rather than shipping past the resign half, so the attribution stays with the originating design, not the fix site.","timestamp":1787438262806376001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787423336383876001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9d8eb1b6-ae63-4d29-a308-8b4eb871488d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ec1e-be67-8774-4eef"},{"link_uuid":"bb5b63a6-f172-4f5f-a9da-3c1ccb638589","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"03c4-d88d-e78b-41c4"},{"link_uuid":"cb865831-0ef0-4190-ba35-890785a6d027","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"5967-4476-7f9f-442d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nParity sibling of ec1e-be67-8774-4eef (staged-index store-read-failure race).\n\nThe primary fix (Gerrit change 2118, commit 1c5d997487d) made `generation.sign_manifest`\nRETRY a transient `store-read-failure` from its pre-lock generation-baseline reads instead\nof aborting terminally, so a peer session's in-flight `git add` -> `git commit` staged index\nno longer blocks signing.\n\nThe `sign-review` recovery path (`resign_plan_review` in src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py,\nthe baseline collect at ~:179) establishes its OWN generation baseline with a single\n`generation.collect(..., ignore_untracked=True)` wrapped in a broad `except Exception` that\nreturns the terminal refusal \"plan review generation could not be collected: <exc>\". A\nconcurrent writer's staged index makes that collect() raise store-read-failure, so\n`sign-review` — the very command meant to recover a PASS-but-unsigned verdict under exactly\nthese conditions — fails the same concurrency race, with no retry.\n\n(resign's SUBSEQUENT signing step, attest.sign_plan_review -> generation.sign_manifest at\nresign.py:349, already inherits the primary retry fix; only the pre-signing collect is\nexposed.)\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror change 2118's retry pattern EXACTLY around resign's baseline collect: extract the\ncollect into a helper that loops `generation.MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS` times, catches\n`PlanRelationSnapshotError`, and on `reason == \"store-read-failure\"` logs a retry event and\nsleeps a jittered per-attempt backoff\n(`random.uniform(0, generation.STORE_READ_RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS * attempt)`) before the next\nattempt — the same bounded attempts / backoff / classification as `sign_manifest`'s loop.\nDeterministic `PlanRelationSnapshotError` reasons (missing/ambiguous/malformed/reducer/\nid-mismatch) and any other exception stay terminal via the existing structured refusal\n(\"plan review generation could not be collected: <exc>\") — resign remains a no-throw API.\nOn exhaustion, return a structured refusal that names the transient store-read-failure and\ntells the caller to retry `rebar sign-review` (retry-after-repair), not the terminal\none-shot message. The helper keeps `resign_plan_review`'s cyclomatic complexity flat\n(complexity-baseline ratchet).\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py — wrap the baseline `generation.collect` in the\n  bounded store-read-failure retry helper.\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py (or test_plan_review_resign.py) — RED->GREEN\n  tests mirroring tests/unit/test_plan_review_sign_transaction.py's `_raising_head` approach,\n  driven through the `resign_plan_review` surface.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests through the resign surface, mirroring test_plan_review_sign_transaction.py:\n- transient store-read-failure (fails once, then clears) -> resign proceeds and signs\n  (`ok=True, signed=True`) — RED under current code (terminal refusal), GREEN after the fix.\n- persistent store-read-failure (never clears) -> exhausts the budget and returns a\n  structured `ok=False` refusal whose reason names the transient store-read-failure and\n  advises retrying sign-review, after exactly MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS collect attempts.\n- deterministic PlanRelationSnapshotError reason (e.g. malformed-reference) -> terminal\n  refusal on the FIRST attempt (no retry).\nRun: `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_sign_transaction.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A transient store-read-failure during resign's baseline collect is retried and, once it\n      clears, sign-review signs (RED->GREEN unit test through the resign_plan_review surface;\n      checked by running the new test against the pre-fix code = RED, post-fix = GREEN).\n- [x] A persistent store-read-failure exhausts the retry budget (MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS)\n      and surfaces as a structured, retry-after-repair refusal naming store-read-failure —\n      not the one-shot terminal \"could not be collected\" abort (checked by unit test\n      asserting the refusal reason and the attempt count).\n- [x] Deterministic PlanRelationSnapshotError reasons (missing/ambiguous/malformed/reducer/\n      id-mismatch) remain terminal on the first attempt (checked by unit test).\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      (new=0 increased=0) pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py","reason":"wrap the baseline generation.collect in a bounded store-read-failure retry mirroring sign_manifest"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign_heldout.py","reason":"RED->GREEN tests for the transient/persistent/deterministic store-read-failure paths through resign_plan_review"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","03c4-d88d-e78b-41c4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"64cffb8d-d73c-4524-998a-6f8b305dab61","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"90c1-c112-d076-4c96","ticket_type":"bug","title":"sign-review baseline collect aborts on transient store-read-failure (parity sibling)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dadc6f8a-c4ba-4f38-a091-3538ab33daab","e3ecd366-8d95-4027-9ea9-83ba80396dac","55f94dd3-c02c-4c8c-9778-b3129e888761","79b438d4-02b7-4f87-99cb-c6160cf501d8","fcb1af0c-c8fc-4702-9fd3-3f5b75406404","7d78211e-7173-4e6d-a4c2-5239ab2e2b92","97b12744-2b69-4a7e-a2e4-d0e66100f540","bb5b63a6-f172-4f5f-a9da-3c1ccb638589","845d1019-ebae-433e-a72d-fe6a6e6348f4","bc181942-f645-4aa8-9d48-08982f0278dd","64cffb8d-d73c-4524-998a-6f8b305dab61","709d1c27-2834-4672-9024-4c69c6251ada","cb865831-0ef0-4190-ba35-890785a6d027"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787454372250875001,"uuid":"b5557f7b-0337-44a6-8f91-9f3b0efb5a53"}